{"id":"43afe63c-e5e5-4d2b-8436-12c9703d7ba7","revision":0,"last_node_id":41,"last_link_id":59,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-420],"size":[3840,360],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · Storyboard to video with sound — FastH3 OmniRef (MiniMax H3, 8 steps)\n\nThree trees with the same shape drive one batch of clips: the **keyframes** (Load Media: one named group per scene — the sample keyframes that come with Arbor), a **motion** line per shot and a **sound** line per scene.\n\n1. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) writes one prompt per shot in the structured format FastH3 OmniRef expects — subject definitions, summary, shot description, soundscape. Motion and sound are both one branch per scene, in the same order: the branches pair up and the scene's sound line repeats for each of its shots (longest list) — Grasshopper's data matching. `{name}` is the scene.\n2. **Tree to Data** flattens the keyframes: each one is `<Picture 1>` — the reference image — of its own clip in **MiniMax H3 Reference to Video**, which generates picture **and** sound.\n3. FastH3 OmniRef renders in **8 steps**. Keep **Model Sparse Attention** on *vsa* (keep 10 %) and **SigmaShift** at 12 / 3: the checkpoint is trained for them.\n4. **Construct Tree** with the keyframe tree as its *structure* puts the clips back into scenes: **Save by Path** files them one folder per scene (`output/arbor/h3/0 · Arrival/000.mp4 …`), **Video Grid** plays them all at once (a row per scene, a column per shot), and **Batch Pick** `0, -1` + a second **Construct Tree** make a contact sheet of first and last frames.\n\nClips are 124 frames (~5 s, the shortest the model is trained for) at 0.4 MP to keep the demo quick — raise the resolution for real shots. Use your own keyframes with **Add…** on Load Media (a folder: every subfolder becomes a scene)."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · Storyboard to video with sound — FastH3 OmniRef (MiniMax H3, 8 steps)\n\nThree trees with the same shape drive one batch of clips: the **keyframes** (Load Media: one named group per scene — the sample keyframes that come with Arbor), a **motion** line per shot and a **sound** line per scene.\n\n1. **Prompt Template** (*zip*) writes one prompt per shot in the structured format FastH3 OmniRef expects — subject definitions, summary, shot description, soundscape. Motion and sound are both one branch per scene, in the same order: the branches pair up and the scene's sound line repeats for each of its shots (longest list) — Grasshopper's data matching. `{name}` is the scene.\n2. **Tree to Data** flattens the keyframes: each one is `<Picture 1>` — the reference image — of its own clip in **MiniMax H3 Reference to Video**, which generates picture **and** sound.\n3. FastH3 OmniRef renders in **8 steps**. Keep **Model Sparse Attention** on *vsa* (keep 10 %) and **SigmaShift** at 12 / 3: the checkpoint is trained for them.\n4. **Construct Tree** with the keyframe tree as its *structure* puts the clips back into scenes: **Save by Path** files them one folder per scene (`output/arbor/h3/0 · Arrival/000.mp4 …`), **Video Grid** plays them all at once (a row per scene, a column per shot), and **Batch Pick** `0, -1` + a second **Construct Tree** make a contact sheet of first and last frames.\n\nClips are 124 frames (~5 s, the shortest the model is trained for) at 0.4 MP to keep the demo quick — raise the resolution for real shots. Use your own keyframes with **Add…** on Load Media (a folder: every subfolder becomes a scene)."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":2,"type":"Arbor_LoadMedia","pos":[0,0],"size":[420,363],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"files"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"文件","name":"files","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":[32,36,38]},{"localized_name":"图片","name":"images","type":"ARBOR_TREE","links":null},{"localized_name":"视频",